{"path":"cargo/getting-started/installation.html","title":"Installation","description":"The easiest way to get Cargo is to install the current stable release of Rust by using rustup. Installing Rust using rustup will also install cargo.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"install-rust-and-cargo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install Rust and Cargo"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The easiest way to get Cargo is to install the current stable release of "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.rust-lang.org/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rust"}]},{"type":"text","value":" by using "},{"type":"link","href":"https://rustup.rs/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"rustup"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Installing Rust using "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"rustup"},{"type":"text","value":" will also install "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Linux and macOS systems, this is done as follows:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"curl https://sh.rustup.rs -sSf | sh"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It will download a script, and start the installation. If everything goes well, you’ll see this appear:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"Rust is installed now. Great!"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Windows, download and run "},{"type":"link","href":"https://win.rustup.rs/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"rustup-init.exe"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It will start the installation in a console and present the above message on success."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After this, you can use the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"rustup"},{"type":"text","value":" command to also install "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"beta"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"nightly"},{"type":"text","value":" channels for Rust and Cargo."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For other installation options and information, visit the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"install"}]},{"type":"text","value":" page of the Rust website."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"build-and-install-cargo-from-source","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build and Install Cargo from Source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, you can "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo#compiling-from-source","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"build Cargo from source"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}}
